WEBVTT

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.300
The equivalent of a Welle Shield...

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.940
That's an impressive barrier.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.290
Kazuki, hit it with an opposing wavelength!

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.110
Got it.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.250
Assimilation won't work?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.750
I'm going to get a read on its data.
Buy me five seconds.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.400
I've located the core...

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:40.350
Oh, no!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.120
Use your power for defense!

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.580
The mechs might hold out,

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.130
but we won't!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.760
The Mir is protecting us...

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.560
If it hadn't, that blast would've annihilated us.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.330
Kazuki-kun!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.070
Don't, Toumi-senpai!

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.980
There's nothing we can do!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.720
Kazuki!

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.430
What's wrong, Mark Nicht?

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.650
Is this all the child of nothingness can do?!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.860
Disappear!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.280
Kazuki, can you move?

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.270
Yeah...

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.070
I can keep going.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.240
The mech regenerated...

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.020
I'm giving it the factor, to prevent
it from materializing.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.970
That won't finish it, but it should stop its movement!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.400
Kazuki, destroy the enemy core!

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.130
What is that?

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.950
They defeated the Diablo-type and the Azazel-type.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.370
And they saved our assimilated comrades.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.780
They even managed to get the ROE Alpha revoked.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.790
How many miracles have we seen here?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:04.240
The power to save humanity... To save the world.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.050
The Azazel-type is down.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.590
The enemy swarm is falling apart!

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.260
All troops are to aid the wounded.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:15.430
The damage is massive.
Verify the status of all regions.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.620
Makabe Fumihiko,

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.040
I thank you for using your power
to save yourselves.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:25.110
For the use of your own child.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:31.780
Are Kazuki-oniichan and Soushi-oniichan
going to go away?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.160
They're still fine.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.540
But if they continue to use the power,

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.170
it will eventually assimilate them.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.380
I didn't know.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.290
They both came of their own free wills.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.750
For you and your friend.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.300
Come on, let's ask them.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:53.790
Okay.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.780
The core we needed to dispose of escaped.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.390
It's an offshoot of the Mir.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.890
Tracking it down would take time.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.390
If it comes back, we'll beat it then.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.070
What's that voice?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.540
Please...

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.720
Miwa-chan?

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:11.990
Crossing?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.160
How many people's voices are getting
through with no system?

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:20.460
Please... Protect everyone.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.840
"Everyone"? There are tens of thousands.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:37.150
She's asking us to protect all of them?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:26.820
Soushi-senpai!

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.660
You're amazing! I can't believe
you can use Nicht!

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.490
I'm glad you're both safe.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.660
Toumi, thanks for holding out.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.540
Why didn't you stop Kazuki-kun?

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.710
I won't make excuses for letting him pilot it.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.630
Sorry... I know you didn't have a choice.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.250
Toumi...

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.600
Kazuki-kun...

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.520
Thank you for saving me, Kazuki-kun...

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.870
You should apologize to her and to me.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.090
Why to you?

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.950
I'm always the one she cries on,

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:21.930
but you get the thanks.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.620
Doesn't that sound unfair?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.040
What are you talking about?

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.210
Kazuki-oniichan!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.130
Soushi-oniichan!

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.550
Miwa-chan?

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:38.090
I believed you'd come.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.620
Did the Mir make her grow?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.080
Yes, but it's all right.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.770
The Mir understands that any further growth

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.440
would endanger her life.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.600
Yumiko-sensei...

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.530
You saved our lives. Makabe's orders?

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.390
Yes, and the core told us to.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.120
The core?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:03.020
Miwa-chan used the Mir here to tell
the island's Mir about the danger.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:06.830
So the island's core awoke and sent us here.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.810
The core... You mean Minashiro Tsubaki?

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.130
She woke up?

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:15.120
She isn't Tsubaki. She was given
the name "Minashiro Orihime."

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.050
She's a new being, with a new personality.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.830
The situation's changed quite a bit.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.720
So, what were you ordered to do from here?

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.990
To do as Miwa-chan wishes.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:29.560
If you don't protect everyone,

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.950
when the big star comes, it'll be even worse.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.910
As you can see, the town is destroyed.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.570
Local forces are working to help,

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:46.260
and we're doing everything we can to assist!

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:56.760
After this, hating the enemy is only natural.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.810
Don't... We aren't doing this to perpetuate
that sort of sentiment.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.640
It isn't like I came here to watch this!

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.970
I'm glad I came here.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.490
Every human suffers, no matter who it is.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:15.820
We should help each other. This is no
time to fight amongst ourselves.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.070
How many are we supposed to save?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:22.370
The Human Army would fire upon their
own without a second thought.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.410
Isn't it more important to protect our island?!

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.330
We will be protecting our island.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.480
Miwa-chan is right.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.810
If we all hate each other, no one will be left.

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:35.410
Neither people nor Festum.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.130
I'm alive?

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.270
Yeah.

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.690
I felt Makabe's presence.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:12:01.110
I was assimilated, and he saved me...

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:03.490
We were all saved.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:08.290
By the D Island soldiers and by the Salvator-model.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.250
Emery!

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:13.440
Miwa!

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:24.180
I'm sorry... I was supposed to protect
you, but you saved everyone.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.600
No, without you, I couldn't have done anything.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.950
Sis...

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.360
Is this Michio-san's?

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.870
It belonged to Miwa's father, so I
brought it for protection...

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.830
But I can't use it now.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:55.250
Sis, what's wrong?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.670
What? You don't need to worry about me.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:02.950
You haven't slept in a long time,
have you? Have you eaten?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.320
Should I bring you something to eat?

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:08.030
It's all right. Right now, I don't need anything.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.520
Maya, you carry this.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.220
Huh?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.350
You've learned to use one, haven't you? Please.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:18.230
Okay...

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.250
We must abandon this place.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.670
The town was left to fight alone, and it fell.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:30.450
If we send a message anywhere now,
the enemy will come before our allies can.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.370
Regarding communication, the candidates
have already departed.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:35.840
Departed?

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.650
They're going to send a message

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:41.550
from somewhere far away, so it won't
matter if they attract the enemy?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.330
That's a harsh mission...

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:46.760
If we don't send word that we've survived
and fought off the enemy,

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.840
ROE Alpha will be declared.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:53.650
It's the rule of attack for regions and
people who have been assimilated.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.480
The survivors, too?

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.400
Abandon this place? What about the Mir?

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:02.320
The Mir's core will travel with us.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.490
We'll allow it to mature further in a safe location,

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.680
then attempt communication with Altair again.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.410
What safe location?

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:12.350
A place the Mir's core and the
Esperanto discovered together.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.650
Only certain individuals can be told where.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.530
Even I don't know yet.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.580
Why keep it a secret?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:24.510
You think they're close,
the traitor who brought all this on.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.050
There's no definite proof.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:30.680
Emery has mind-reading power
on par with that of a Festum,

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.180
yet she can't find the traitor.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.570
There's no proof that there isn't one, either.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:39.000
That's right. We don't want to jump
at shadows and create chaos.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.100
Naturally.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:44.770
But with our destination secret,
how do we get there?

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:49.280
First, we'll head for the Dhaka base,
the South Asian fleet's flagship base.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:54.370
We'll secure forces and take only those that
wish to migrate to the new world.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.420
That's about 2,500 kilometers.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.320
In a transport craft, it'd take no time.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.500
There are approximately 22,000 survivors.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.440
There are multiple elderly and
children among the wounded.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:08.900
We'll transport the people by car,
and supplies by transport craft.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.870
We'll only travel within safe zones,

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.850
so according to our calculations,
it should take about two weeks.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:16.510
How many will you take to protect all those people?

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:20.830
We'll have 42 Fafners, 320 soldiers,

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.440
and 100 exceptionally brilliant Esperantos.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.700
So you'll have one Fafner for every 500 people?

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.580
Then whenever one Fafner is lost,

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.990
that's 500 people who'll be left unprotected.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:38.010
I apologize for bringing these
circumstances upon us.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:42.150
It would be possible for you two
alone to return to the island.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.090
But as a commander...

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.120
As a man, I want to ask for your help.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:51.040
I want you to protect our path,

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.180
protect our hope.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:01.600
Makabe!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.270
Hey.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.440
I'm glad you're okay.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.410
I promised you I'd protect them.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.030
I don't know how to apologize.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.700
You don't need to apologize.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.570
You saved everyone,

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.090
even the ones who were assimilated.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.870
On behalf of my comrades, I thank you.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.650
I didn't...

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:23.730
We did it for our brethren.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:28.040
It's a tragedy that lives were lost.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:32.020
Those of us who survived will do our best.

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:35.720
And... What will you guys do now?

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.150
Nothing's decided yet. We're heading back to report.

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.940
That's right. Sorry, but we have to go.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:42.700
Wait!

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.890
Please tell me...

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:47.730
Would it be possible for us
to have mechs like yours?

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:49.810
Not likely.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.050
Those mechs can destroy allies,
including their own pilots.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.160
By all rights, they should be sealed away.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:58.070
I see...

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.530
See you later.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:07.360
But I can test to find out if it's possible...

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.300
Using my own life.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.840
Right, Makabe?

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.150
Protect 22,000 people?

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.200
That's ten times the number
of people on the island.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.500
There's no way!

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:27.880
But the guys took out the enemy boss.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.520
We might not see any enemies.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.360
No.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.380
There are many other Azazel-types.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:38.750
As long as the general and his men attempt
to communicate with the approaching Mir,

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.160
the enemy will pursue us.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.790
This isn't something we should be doing.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.640
What did Miwa-chan say?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:47.320
She says she's going with everyone else.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.340
My sister said that's for the best, too.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.370
I'll go, as well.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:54.850
We've gotta do something about
the enemy coming from space.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.670
Is something like that really coming?

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.390
Here you go.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.310
Rakuen's own blend. It's tasty.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.560
Can Miwa-chan speak with the island's core?

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.970
It's a power she can use precisely because
the Mir here is alive and well.

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:14.230
Right now, it would be difficult.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.900
Using a high-speed craft to report
to the island is our only choice.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:22.830
Let's decide whether we're going to
follow them or withdraw here!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.170
Why do you have that?

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:39.030
Oh... Well...

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:41.000
It's Michio-san's.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.770
My sister told me to carry it.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:48.020
I've been trained, so...

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:51.610
Sorry I couldn't wait on the island.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.980
Minashiro-kun told you to say that, didn't he?

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.940
W-Well, he said I should apologize.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:02.200
I just felt so helpless...

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.870
I started thinking I didn't want
to see anyone else sacrificed,

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.950
and that I could take your place.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.870
I know I don't have that kind of strength.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:16.780
You fought more than well enough, Toumi.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.850
I want you to go back to the island with the others.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:21.740
We'll take care of Miwa-chan.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:23.640
I can't leave my family!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.590
I came this far from home,

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:34.680
but I couldn't find what you wished for.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.210
I'm sorry.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.380
We'll find it.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.660
You think I should drag Miwa-chan back home?

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:46.810
Fighting so hard for a bunch of
people we don't even know...

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:52.520
It'd be so much easier just to find our own peace.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:56.790
Miwa-chan can see things we can't.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:00.090
I want to believe in her.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:01.800
Yeah.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:06.360
I'll protect the people here, same as the island.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.710
I don't know if that will really bring peace.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.230
It's just what I want to do.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:16.950
Yeah.

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.530
It's what I want to do, too.

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:56.270
Let us set forth for a new land,

00:20:56.660 --> 00:21:00.010
to enable our Mir to blossom once again.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:18.930
Let's have faith that this town
will be restored someday.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:25.800
The island is probably on the
move to go into battle.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.510
Let them pick up our coordinates.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:29.220
Roger!

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.140
We'll be heading home first.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.820
Start up brigade control!

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:53.980
To avoid congestion, the land transport
team will split into three groups.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:56.780
Transport crafts will divide into
front and rear positions,

00:21:56.780 --> 00:21:59.650
and maintain those at the same
speed as the vehicles'.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:06.380
The condition of the path we'll travel is unknown.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.060
Maintain reason and order,

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:09.840
and be flexible at all times.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:13.070
Let's go!

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:19.880
And so, we left the destroyed town

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:21.990
for a new land,

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.360
not even knowing the price of hope.

00:22:25.810 --> 00:22:28.640
Moving ahead, we kept faith that
we could protect the people,

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:33.800
as the journey to sacrifice everything began.

00:24:05.860 --> 00:24:09.220
